{# On the council's agenda.

   SEPARATE FROM COUNCIL CORNER, DELIBERATELY. Council corner is the
   Community Council's own record, drawn only from their approved minutes,
   and nothing writes into it from anywhere else. This page is drawn only
   from North Ayrshire's committee papers and meeting calendar. Different
   source, different tense, no cross-reference between them. If a reader
   notices the same subject in both, that is their inference to draw, not
   this site's claim to make.

   WHAT THIS PAGE KNOWS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT. It knows a meeting is
   happening, whether papers have been lodged, and whether the word Largs
   appears in them. It has not read a single document. So every row says
   "mentions" and links out — it never characterises, summarises or ranks.
   A page that guessed at substance would be worth less than nothing here.

   Links go to the MEETING PAGE, not the file. The meeting page lists the
   agenda items and survives; document links are 600-character encrypted
   tokens that may not.

   No JavaScript. The folds are <details>, which is markup, not script. #}

<div class="wrap">
{% if not agenda.ok %}
  <p class="agenda-empty">The agenda list has not been collected yet, so there is
  nothing to show. This page will fill in once it has run.</p>
{% else %}

<p class="agenda-intro">North Ayrshire Council publishes the papers for its
committees at least three days before each meeting. This page lists the ones
that mention Largs, so you can see what is coming before it is decided rather
than after. Some mentions are decisions about the town; others are just the name
in a list. Follow the link to see which.</p>

<h2>Coming up</h2>
{% if agenda.upcoming | length %}
  <ul class="agenda-list">
  {% for m in agenda.upcoming %}
    <li class="agenda-row agenda-ahead">
      <p class="agenda-when">{{ m.display }}</p>
      <p class="agenda-what">
        {% if m.url %}<a href="{{ m.url }}">{{ m.committee }}</a>
        {% else %}{{ m.committee }}{% endif %}
      </p>
      <p class="agenda-detail">{{ m.hits }} mention{% if m.hits != 1 %}s{% endif %}
      of Largs in the papers.</p>
    </li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ul>
{% else %}
  <p class="agenda-none">No meeting with published papers mentions Largs at the
  moment. Papers appear about three days before a meeting, so this is the normal
  state between sittings.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if agenda.counts.scheduled %}
<p class="agenda-forward"><a href="/on-the-agenda/scheduled/">{{ agenda.counts.scheduled }}
more meetings are in the council's diary{% if agenda.scheduledTo %}, up to
{{ agenda.scheduledTo }}{% endif %} →</a><br>
<span class="agenda-sub">Their papers are not published yet, so there is no way
to know yet whether Largs is in them.</span></p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Recently</h2>
{% if agenda.recent | length %}
  <ul class="agenda-list">
  {% for m in agenda.recent %}
    <li class="agenda-row">
      <p class="agenda-when">{{ m.display }}</p>
      <p class="agenda-what">
        {% if m.url %}<a href="{{ m.url }}">{{ m.committee }}</a>
        {% else %}{{ m.committee }}{% endif %}
      </p>
      <p class="agenda-detail">{{ m.hits }} mention{% if m.hits != 1 %}s{% endif %}
      in the papers</p>
    </li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ul>
{% else %}
  <p class="agenda-none">Nothing in the last {{ agenda.recentDays }} days.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if agenda.earlier | length %}
<details class="agenda-earlier">
  <summary>Earlier meetings ({{ agenda.earlier | length }})</summary>
  <ul class="agenda-list">
  {% for m in agenda.earlier %}
    <li class="agenda-row">
      <p class="agenda-when">{{ m.display }}</p>
      <p class="agenda-what">
        {% if m.url %}<a href="{{ m.url }}">{{ m.committee }}</a>
        {% else %}{{ m.committee }}{% endif %}
      </p>
      <p class="agenda-detail">{{ m.hits }} mention{% if m.hits != 1 %}s{% endif %}
      in the papers</p>
    </li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</details>
{% endif %}

<details class="agenda-how">
  <summary>How this page is made</summary>
  <p>Two lists are put together. North Ayrshire publishes a calendar of its
  committee meetings months in advance, which is where the dates come from. It
  also runs a search across its own committee documents, which is where the
  mention counts come from. Nothing here is written by hand, and nothing is
  interpreted.</p>
  <p>A mention can be substantial or trivial. A town name in a list of
  settlements counts the same as a decision about the town, and there is no way
  to tell which is which without opening the paper. That is why this page points
  rather than summarises.</p>
  <p>Papers are normally published at least three days before a meeting, so a
  meeting listed without papers is not being ignored — the documents simply do
  not exist yet. Minutes follow afterwards.</p>
  {% if agenda.counts %}
  <p class="agenda-meta">{{ agenda.counts.meetings }} meetings known,
  {{ agenda.counts.mentioned }} with papers mentioning Largs{% if agenda.cutoff %},
  back to {{ agenda.cutoff }}{% endif %}.</p>
  {% endif %}
</details>

<p class="agenda-note">This is not the Community Council's record. What Largs
Community Council itself discussed, and what it is still pursuing, is in
<a href="/council/">Council corner</a>.</p>

{% endif %}
</div>
